import { EffectSequencingCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> EffectSequencingCopy = EffectSequencingCopy {
  summary: "Provide a fallback for an expected failure, such as a missing setting.",
  taskTitle: "Use a preview title when a setting is missing",
  purpose: "Keep a saved title, use Preview only when the setting is missing, and reject a broken setting. The important decision is to distinguish missing from invalid setting rather than replace every failure with a default.",
  typescriptBefore: "The TypeScript version returns an ordinary success-or-failure object. An if statement replaces the result only when its reason is missing. It makes the same decision with normal branching, without throwing an exception.",
  benefit: "recover keeps the failure decision in fallback. If the original operation succeeds, its value passes through and fallback is not called.",
  setup: "The std/effect import makes the helpers available under effects. lookup and fallback are ordinary functions that take a string and return an operation to run.",
  after: [
    "lookup returns Effect<{}, String, String>: an operation needing no additional environment, with String for both its expected failure and its successful value. effects.succeed represents success; effects.fail represents an expected failure. The success or failure side distinguishes what each string means.",
    "In effects.recover fallback (lookup key), fallback receives the reason if the original operation fails. A function called later this way is a callback. For missing, it chooses an operation producing Preview. Otherwise, effects.fail reason preserves the failure.",
    "effects.attempt turns success or an expected failure from that operation into an Either<String, String> value. Right carries the successful value; Left carries the failure reason. Either case can then reach the display decision.",
    "describe is an ordinary function. match selects the Right or Left case and names its contents value or reason. The function adds Title: or Rejected: and returns the resulting string.",
    "The do block in effect fn display runs operations in order. result <- runs attempt and receives its successful value, which is an Either. In main, _ <- runs display and discards its result; it does not ignore a failure.",
    "saved produces Release, missing produces Preview, and broken produces Rejected: invalid setting. The last display is main's final operation. These cases separately demonstrate an allowed fallback and a setting that must remain rejected."
  ],
  details: [
    "A common mistake is returning Preview for every reason and hiding an invalid setting. Branch only on reasons that permit a fallback, and return the others as failures, as effects.fail reason does here.",
    "fallback must return an operation rather than a bare string. Wrap a replacement value with effects.succeed. recover handles only the expected failures represented by the error type; runtime defects and cancellation bypass this callback.",
    "attempt surrounds lookup and recover, not the later println. Output itself can still fail. Without attempt, an unrecovered expected failure would propagate to the surrounding operation instead of becoming a Left value for describe."
  ]
}
